    "title": "Why wasn't Sean Penn at the Oscars? Winner didn't show",
    "text": "AdvertisementAdvertisementReturn to HomepageEntertainment: 'Survivor' surprise double-eliminationPlay Crushable by Candy CrushNew 'Harry Potter' series nameTaylor Frankie Paul backlashDuffer Brothers' new project'Sad Affleck' meme backstory'KPop Demon Hunters' happy meals'Harry Potter' series trailerMorgan Stewart on podcastingAndrew McCarthy's journeyBill for scrapped 'Bachelorette'Veteran actor Sean Penn won his third Oscar on Sunday night in Hollywood for his villainous turn as Col. Steven J. Lockjaw in Paul Thomas Anderson's One Battle After Another.However, Penn was not in attendance to accept his Best Supporting Actor Oscar. Where was he?The New York Times shared that Penn was in Europe for a planned trip to Ukraine at the same time as this year's ceremony.Why didn't he attend? Penn has been vocal about his support for Ukraine during the war, so he may have felt it more important to be there. It's also very possible Penn just did not want to attend the ceremony.AdvertisementAdvertisementHe was not present at the Actor Awards earlier this month, nor did he attend the BAFTAs in February. He's just not been as interested this go-around in attending the big shows.We're sure they'll get Penn his third Oscar statue, but it doesn't appear as if he's all that interested in winning one.Alas!This article originally appeared on For The Win: Why wasn't Sean Penn at the Oscars? Winner didn't showView comments(2)AdvertisementAdvertisementTerms and Privacy PolicyYour Privacy ChoicesAbout Our AdsTerms and Privacy PolicyYour Privacy ChoicesAbout Our AdsRecommended articlesAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisement",
